IO-20: report an invalid [SUBAREAS] number as ERROR 211, not ERROR 209

subcatch_readSubareaParams() reports a non-numeric or negative Manning's n,
depression storage or PctZero with ERR_NAME, "ERROR 209: undefined object
abc", which sends the user looking for a missing object. Use ERR_NUMBER
("ERROR 211: invalid number"), as every other numeric check in the file
does.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-20_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/subcatch.c b/src/legacy/engine/subcatch.c
index 7c1d97c..14aafce 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/subcatch.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/subcatch.c
@@ -239,7 +239,7 @@ int subcatch_readSubareaParams(char* tok[], int ntoks)
     for (i = 0; i < 5; i++)
     {
         if ( ! getDouble(tok[i+1], &x[i])  || x[i] < 0.0 )
-            return error_setInpError(ERR_NAME, tok[i+1]);
+            return error_setInpError(ERR_NUMBER, tok[i+1]);
     }
 
     // --- check for valid runoff routing keyword
